THIRD-PARTY DATA INCLUDED IN THIS ARTIFACT

data/universe.csv is derived from the Wikipedia article "List of S&P 500 companies", retrieved
2026-07-31 via the MediaWiki API, and data/sp500_wikipedia_rev1365256480.wikitext.gz is the
unmodified wikitext of revision 1365256480 of that article (dated 2026-07-21, the live revision
on the retrieval date; https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=1365256480). Wikipedia text is
licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/); both files are
redistributed under the same licence, with attribution to the Wikipedia contributors listed in the
article history.

data/prices.csv.gz is derived from the Yahoo Finance chart endpoint. It is included for
reproducibility of the analysis in this paper only; redistribution or commercial use may be
restricted by Yahoo's terms of service, and users should obtain their own price data for any other
purpose.

data/scores.jsonl and data/scores_probe.jsonl are outputs of open-weight models run locally. The
model builds, with content digests and quantisation levels, are recorded in
data/model_provenance.json. Each model carries its own upstream licence. data/scores_or.jsonl holds
outputs of nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b, obtained through OpenRouter's free tier in August
2026; the model's own licence and OpenRouter's terms apply to them.

Filing text is from SEC EDGAR and is in the public domain. The SEC requires automated access to
identify itself: set the SEC_CONTACT environment variable to your own email address before running
code/collect.py. The default placeholder is not a valid contact string and running with it would
breach the SEC's access policy.
